  "findings": [
    "Default -1 participated in v2 profiling and won2/3cold trials at each shape: M128 seeds18/19 and M144 seeds17/18. All four winners survived fresh file reloads as genuine hits.",
    "M128 warm v2/v1 latency is0.9902773854189744 eager and1.0142401094145443 graph by median paired ratio. All three sampled warm graph ratios exceed1.",
    "M144 warm v2/v1 latency is1.0156243832206233 eager and0.9207490623620652 graph. All three sampled eager ratios exceed1; graph is faster in two trials and slower in seed19.",
    "M144 warm same-sweep graph selected-to-best ratios have medians1.086357850516837 for v1 and1.0139067331584284 for v2. This improves the measured candidate-ranking diagnostic while natural eager latency still regresses.",
    "M144 seed19 v2 selected the same explicit descriptor as v1. Its warm graph selected-to-best oracle ratio is1.079343897180164. This is an exploratory measured ranking, not proof that the algorithm is universally suboptimal.",
    "The default true-miss versus cached eager gap includes lookup/dispatch-path differences. It does not isolate GPU algorithm quality; cached-default oracle timing is the appropriate same-tier candidate comparison.",
    "Results support correct candidate adoption and persistence, with performance depending on shape, mode and trial. They do not establish uniform v2 superiority or a serving speedup."
  ],
  "diagnostic_and_causal_distinctions": [
    "Natural paired latency is the observed public-operation outcome; selected-to-best oracle ratios assess measured candidate quality within the same worker, sweep and lookup tier.",
    "Natural-versus-oracle comparisons span separate timing windows and may be below1; they are not pure selection regret.",
    "Taking the minimum of nine noisy candidate estimates makes the measured oracle optimistic. Minimum-selection noise, execution order, clock and sampling variation contribute to small apparent regret.",
    "Observed winner/runner-up profiler gaps are roughly1.1\u20133.0percent in these v2 trials. Current data do not isolate noise versus a mismatch between profiling and eventual runtime objectives.",
    "All867actual profiling rows record use_cuda_graph=False and use_cold_l2_cache=False. The measurement policy remained unspecified; no explicit eager/graph policy or cold-L2 override was tested. CUDA Graph replay was evaluated separately at runtime.",
    "Startup intervals exclude explicit native compilation/build and the initial untuned public call, but include wrapper tuning work. They are secondary diagnostics and are not full-server startup measurements."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Three independent fresh-worker trials per comparison, not45; 15samples estimate each worker latency.",
    "One H100 NVL, two small FP8 shapes and an experimental source overlay; no confidence interval, significance, equivalence or broad performance guarantee.",
    "No direct absolute performance comparison with previous HBM3 batches.",
    "No model-serving, BF16, distributed, managed-store, explicit-policy or production rollout qualification.",
    "All324oracle candidates were accepted here; this does not establish acceptance for other shapes or devices.",
    "Descriptor enumeration indices are diagnostics local to each worker; the persisted tactics are the full descriptors."
  ],
  "next_recommendation": {
    "immediate": "Publish the complete mixed results and retain the existing v1 baseline/persistence; this batch justifies neither removing v1 nor making a serving-performance claim.",
    "conditional_follow_up": "If continuing performance investigation, make the next bounded experiment a ranking-stability and objective-match check on M144's default versus the selected explicit descriptor, retaining eager and graph outcomes separately.",
    "proposed_method": "Use randomized/interleaved paired candidate measurements with the same real file lookup, fixed inputs and numerical guards; repeat fresh tuning trials, report uncertainty and profiler margins, and check whether ranking disagreement persists.",
